\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  Warms the purge before it meets the wash water.

  Not decoration: the purge leaves the separator at 250 K, and you cannot
  scrub a 250 K gas with water -- the water would freeze on the packing.  In a
  real plant this is done against cooling water, which at 298 K is the HOT side
  here; a single-stream heater keeps the case simple.  Q is the spec, T_out is
  the result.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
type      heater;
operation { Q 9500 W; }
boundary  { inlets ( Feed );  outlets ( Out ); }
